  "declared_gap": "TWO declared gaps, neither verified away. (1) org.json escapes '/' after '<' and some non-ASCII ranges as \\uXXXX where json.dumps does not, so a vendor string containing them WOULD diverge. (2) Java Double.toString only guarantees a shortest-round-trip rendering from JDK 19, so a DERIVED non-exact double (such as a raw IV difference) could render with different digits than Python repr on an older JDK. No vector depends on either: every float here is integral or a short literal, and the one derived value is exact in binary. Real records CAN contain both shapes, and for those the two implementations are untested, not proven equal.",
